  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Use lean beef or horse meat. Remove fat and connective tissue before grinding. Mix meat, water, and NaOH and bring to a boil while stirring."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Cool to room temperature, skim fat off surface, and filter, retaining both meat particles and filtrate."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Add sufficient distilled water to filtrate to restore 1 liter original volume."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "To the filtrate add:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Boil, cool and add 0.5 g L-cysteine . HCl; adjust pH to 7.0. Under 97% nitrogen, 3% hydrogen, dispense 7 ml over 1 part meat particles to 4-5 parts fluid per test tube."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "Cap with butyl rubber stoppers under N2, H2 and autoclave in press for 15 minutes under fast exhaust."
    }
  ]
}